[[:db/retract 17592186069320 :question/answer-fields 17592186067451] {:db/id "q-49931/selection/ma-v1/05a7b91b9f6f87764fde2fee6a40698ccd3913a3d54ddaaf39ce9f6c47110ed2/8fc110ad5280b0fe770f9c545eb83930f83274de7e596662073f07a04d757e6c" :answer/id #uuid "749fc843-48f0-527e-a3ec-714541da5669" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49931/selection/ma-v1/05a7b91b9f6f87764fde2fee6a40698ccd3913a3d54ddaaf39ce9f6c47110ed2/cc0d5744b24116101fda834d15c3ac1e47e49193bb8d4a4048015b427199a7df" :answer/id #uuid "ea65bade-2b8d-522a-90e3-c916a32c2b79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49931/selection/ma-v1/05a7b91b9f6f87764fde2fee6a40698ccd3913a3d54ddaaf39ce9f6c47110ed2/c4333dcd06534b838c9c946f225a6552f4aa960c0e7e466fd4cba2dbf2c69799" :answer/id #uuid "c8a90771-05b7-57c2-b96b-79f695625f7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-2\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49931/selection/ma-v1/05a7b91b9f6f87764fde2fee6a40698ccd3913a3d54ddaaf39ce9f6c47110ed2/e5cc6922c7d0918a981aa3ad5d1a00e980a8e4c2562aa23bef998341e6d19483" :answer/id #uuid "575f79eb-7853-5c5f-9463-9ed68ed5049d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49931/selection/ma-v1/05a7b91b9f6f87764fde2fee6a40698ccd3913a3d54ddaaf39ce9f6c47110ed2/9ad9ed167fd3a7fb9a3da571c87171a219ab2eb9af8d5be8f6a821351eff23d3" :answer/id #uuid "aae3d2d3-3e5a-59b0-84dc-4108e0428258" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)-2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-49931/selection/ma-v1/05a7b91b9f6f87764fde2fee6a40698ccd3913a3d54ddaaf39ce9f6c47110ed2" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e536120-814a-5b95-a018-c616d8dd2d5d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-49931/selection/ma-v1/05a7b91b9f6f87764fde2fee6a40698ccd3913a3d54ddaaf39ce9f6c47110ed2/cc0d5744b24116101fda834d15c3ac1e47e49193bb8d4a4048015b427199a7df" :answer-field/choices ["q-49931/selection/ma-v1/05a7b91b9f6f87764fde2fee6a40698ccd3913a3d54ddaaf39ce9f6c47110ed2/8fc110ad5280b0fe770f9c545eb83930f83274de7e596662073f07a04d757e6c" "q-49931/selection/ma-v1/05a7b91b9f6f87764fde2fee6a40698ccd3913a3d54ddaaf39ce9f6c47110ed2/cc0d5744b24116101fda834d15c3ac1e47e49193bb8d4a4048015b427199a7df" "q-49931/selection/ma-v1/05a7b91b9f6f87764fde2fee6a40698ccd3913a3d54ddaaf39ce9f6c47110ed2/c4333dcd06534b838c9c946f225a6552f4aa960c0e7e466fd4cba2dbf2c69799" "q-49931/selection/ma-v1/05a7b91b9f6f87764fde2fee6a40698ccd3913a3d54ddaaf39ce9f6c47110ed2/e5cc6922c7d0918a981aa3ad5d1a00e980a8e4c2562aa23bef998341e6d19483" "q-49931/selection/ma-v1/05a7b91b9f6f87764fde2fee6a40698ccd3913a3d54ddaaf39ce9f6c47110ed2/9ad9ed167fd3a7fb9a3da571c87171a219ab2eb9af8d5be8f6a821351eff23d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-49931"] :question/problem "$\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. \n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2})(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-49931/selection/ma-v1/05a7b91b9f6f87764fde2fee6a40698ccd3913a3d54ddaaf39ce9f6c47110ed2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-114946/selection/0cbedd2fdea1d39275c73da73c8b85207d8516865a12c730dc5ea1676b3c98fb" :answer/id #uuid "99bcf369-caca-5778-8888-d4d039dceb38" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4{e}^{5}+3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114946/selection/5031ff772290d0406f5038fa5d705cff0b435b5d4ab945ac5d6494d142f84748" :answer/id #uuid "6440635b-41f4-514c-a064-911b2c515b56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{5}-2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114946/selection/0c907098c1056a1c9bd33ea7383393466fbcc45263c1a1e904628511ae9ffd3c" :answer/id #uuid "686d78c2-8c16-5b3b-928c-528e9bce2020" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17{e}^{5}-2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114946/selection/4b44c0c9f9162a44459a0188a346cdf5dde04f4bfc2b18f9566e5dfe6c74f313" :answer/id #uuid "15dc5f51-f256-5559-818c-de91ad9b9ddf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{5}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114946/selection/9f1d040112d4f503fccf59a368c1236008b6591b83a9d428f119569f72d30b05" :answer/id #uuid "355864bc-5b6a-5489-bda2-cb7928ed1fa7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12{e}^{5}+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114946/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ca7bfb65-4ff6-579f-8fa3-e6b2503ea858" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114946/selection/0c907098c1056a1c9bd33ea7383393466fbcc45263c1a1e904628511ae9ffd3c" :answer-field/choices ["q-114946/selection/0cbedd2fdea1d39275c73da73c8b85207d8516865a12c730dc5ea1676b3c98fb" "q-114946/selection/5031ff772290d0406f5038fa5d705cff0b435b5d4ab945ac5d6494d142f84748" "q-114946/selection/0c907098c1056a1c9bd33ea7383393466fbcc45263c1a1e904628511ae9ffd3c" "q-114946/selection/4b44c0c9f9162a44459a0188a346cdf5dde04f4bfc2b18f9566e5dfe6c74f313" "q-114946/selection/9f1d040112d4f503fccf59a368c1236008b6591b83a9d428f119569f72d30b05"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114946" :question/id #uuid "640a9063-5e5d-5f66-a705-18c7c5b67633" :question/math-academy-id "q-114946" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2} & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=25{x}^{4} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 25{x}^{4}\\text{d}x=5{x}^{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}(5{x}^{5})-\\int (5{x}^{5})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-10\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{4} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{4}\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})(\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\int {x}^{4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{25}+D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-10\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-10(\\frac{{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{25}+D) \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{5}-10D \\\\  & ={x}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{5})+C\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-10D.$ Finally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & ={[{x}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{5})]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =[{e}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+\\frac{2}{5})]-[{1}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{2}{5})] \\\\  & =[{e}^{5}(5-2+\\frac{2}{5})]-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{17{e}^{5}-2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-114946/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98a67346-c2c9-5d22-8adf-479fea81eaa2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114946"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352028/field-1/b5f053b413066e296e04e6299752dd7f5169fe8612199c1036ba06b4617ff399" :answer/id #uuid "c29a15bd-82df-5193-8952-3ea79f3b8217" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi^2-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352028/field-1/a3fe9af3a8ecec66501ff657dc7751949cedb4fce095048dab2e39a3fc9ebec8" :answer/id #uuid "1cb0e201-f1ed-5ed6-8c5b-b090543127b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\pi^2+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352028/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "70d19801-3829-53fc-8712-aa77403b3de1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352028/field-1/b5f053b413066e296e04e6299752dd7f5169fe8612199c1036ba06b4617ff399" :answer-field/choices ["q-352028/field-1/b5f053b413066e296e04e6299752dd7f5169fe8612199c1036ba06b4617ff399" "q-352028/field-1/a3fe9af3a8ecec66501ff657dc7751949cedb4fce095048dab2e39a3fc9ebec8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352028" :question/id #uuid "2be1c0cd-adaf-53aa-b6b4-1aa499097229" :question/math-academy-id "q-352028" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}27{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=27{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=54x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 27{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(27{x}^{2})(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})(54x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+18\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})\\cdot 1\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 27{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+18\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+18(\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+D) \\\\  & =-9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=18D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}27{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={[-9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)]}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =9{(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{2}-2-2 \\\\  & ={\\pi }^{2}-4 \\\\  & ={\\pi }^{2}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352028/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2a41ede-381e-55f6-99e5-1baf1ea348a1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352028"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
